# Line endings are LF in the index AND in every working tree.
#
# Git for Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` in its SYSTEM config, so a
# plain `git worktree add` wrote CRLF here while D:/docxkit itself was
# LF. The mutation tools compare a module's BYTES against a `.pristine`
# snapshot, so that difference reads as "the module changed after this
# run": `mutation_survivors` printed STALE and a replay refused, in a
# worktree where nothing had been edited at all (2026-09-18).
#
# Pinned here rather than left to each checkout's config, because the
# trap is invisible — the tools are right to refuse, and the reason is
# nowhere near them. D:/docxkit's own tree is still mixed from before
# this file existed; it is normalized separately, when no sweep is
# mirroring from it.
* text=auto eol=lf
